    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5kgrxlu",
      "content": "The MSP (Minimum Support Price) is announced by the Cabinet Committee on Economic Affairs (CCEA) based on CACP recommendations. It covers 23 crops (14 Kharif, 6 Rabi, and 2 commercial crops)."
    },
    {
      "id": "2715i50",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Season</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Crops Covered by MSP</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Kharif (14 crops)</p>",
            "<p>Paddy, Jowar, Bajra, Maize, Ragi, Tur (Arhar), Moong, Urad, Groundnut, Sunflower, Soybean, Sesamum, Nigerseed, Cotton</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Rabi (6 crops)</p>",
            "<p>Wheat, Barley, Gram, Masur (Lentil), Mustard/Rapeseed, Safflower</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Commercial Crops (2)</p>",
            "<p>Sugarcane (FRP — Fair and Remunerative Price), Jute</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rwb8tgb",
      "content": "<strong>Important: </strong><em>FRP for sugarcane is announced by CCEA; State Advised Price (SAP) announced by states can be higher. MSP = C2 + 50% as per recommendation.</em>"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "MSP is recommended by CACP but final approval is given by the Cabinet Committee on Economic Affairs (CCEA) chaired by the Prime Minister.",
        "Remember PMFBY insurance premium percentages: 2% for Kharif, 1.5% for Rabi, and 5% for Commercial/Horticultural crops.",
        "Fair and Remunerative Price (FRP) is announced specifically for Sugarcane instead of regular MSP."
      ],
      "id": "zfhpxcx"
    },
